# A "!" line in a .vscodeignore is an unconditional override, not a later
# rule: vsce keeps a file that any "!" matches, whatever else ignored it.
# coboard-vscode's own file records the trap; this is the same trap with one
# sibling package instead of two, because kb-js has to be requirable from the
# installed extension.
#
# What is kept is exactly what a running extension calls: out/*.js is kb-js's
# flat module layer, and its out/test/, .d.ts and .map files are left behind by
# never matching an exception.
.vscode/**
src/**
webview/**
scripts/**
assets/**
out/test/**
node_modules/**
!node_modules/kb-js/package.json
!node_modules/kb-js/out/*.js
.npmrc
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.webview.json
.lapignore
.lap/**
.kb/**
**/*.map
**/.DS_Store
